  "rationale": "No facts yet, so I start from the spec: 50 MSPS requires 1 result/cycle (pipelined or pipelined_m) with Fmax >= 50 MHz, and max_abs_err <= 2^-12 requires accuracy_bits >= 12. Accuracy depends only on data_width/n_iter/guards/rounding, so I focus the search on the accuracy region that just meets or exceeds 12 bits (W=14-18, N=12-18, round) and let the optimizer trade power vs accuracy_bits. I split budget between the full pipeline (lowest power, but Fmax risk) and pipelined_m (m=2-4) to cover the Fmax-recovery trade-off. Rounding is fixed to 'round' since it strictly improves accuracy at negligible cost, freeing the search to explore the power/accuracy trade-off rather than wasting evaluations on truncation."
